@{ ViewData["Title"] = "About Us"; }
<main class="about-page">
<section class="about-hero">
 <div class="about-container about-hero-grid">
  <div class="about-hero-content">
   <span class="about-eyebrow">ABOUT MEDISYNC</span>
   <h1>Connected healthcare workflows, <span>simplified.</span></h1>
   <p>MediSync is a student-built Healthcare Coordination &amp; Management System designed to connect front-desk operations, appointments, doctor consultations, medical records, laboratory workflows and pharmacy management in one role-based platform.</p>
   <div class="about-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Login">Explore MediSync</a><a class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-lg" href="#team">Meet the Team</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="about-hero-card"><div class="about-hero-icon">✚</div><h2>One workflow. Connected care.</h2><p>From registration to consultation, lab results and prescription dispensing, each role works within its own secure part of the same patient journey.</p><div class="about-stats"><div><strong>6</strong><span>Roles</span></div><div><strong>1</strong><span>Connected workflow</span></div><div><strong>∞</strong><span>Scalable idea</span></div></div></div>
 </div>
</section>
<section class="about-section"><div class="about-container"><div class="about-heading"><span class="about-eyebrow">WHAT IS MEDISYNC?</span><h2>Healthcare coordination organized around the patient journey.</h2><p>MediSync brings operational and clinical workflows together instead of treating appointments, records, laboratory work and pharmacy activity as disconnected modules.</p></div><div class="about-story-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Register</h3><p>Reception handles patient registration and appointment coordination.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Consult</h3><p>Doctors confirm appointments, document consultations and create medical records.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Coordinate</h3><p>Laboratory and pharmacy teams process the next steps in the same workflow.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="about-mission"><div class="about-container"><div><span class="about-eyebrow">OUR MISSION</span><h2>Make healthcare coordination clearer, safer and easier to manage.</h2><p>The project focuses on role-based access, connected workflows, ownership checks and practical validation so every user sees the information and actions relevant to their responsibility.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="about-section"><div class="about-container"><div class="about-heading centered"><span class="about-eyebrow">WHAT MEDISYNC OFFERS</span><h2>Built around real workflow boundaries.</h2></div><div class="about-feature-grid"><article><div class="feature-icon">📅</div><h3>Appointments</h3><p>Scheduling with doctor availability, 15-minute slots and double-booking protection.</p></article><article><div class="feature-icon">🩺</div><h3>Medical Records</h3><p>Doctor-owned consultation records connected to completed appointments.</p></article><article><div class="feature-icon">🧪</div><h3>Laboratory</h3><p>Requests, processing, results and controlled status transitions.</p></article><article><div class="feature-icon">💊</div><h3>Pharmacy</h3><p>Prescription processing with automatic stock deduction and stock protection.</p></article><article><div class="feature-icon">🔐</div><h3>Role Security</h3><p>Six roles with controller-level authorization and patient ownership checks.</p></article><article><div class="feature-icon">📊</div><h3>Dashboards</h3><p>Role-specific dashboards surface the tasks and information each team needs.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="about-tech-section" id="technology"><div class="about-container"><div class="about-heading centered"><span class="about-eyebrow">HOW WE BUILT IT</span><h2>Modern .NET technologies behind the platform.</h2><p>MediSync is built as an ASP.NET Core MVC application with a relational data layer and Identity-based authentication.</p></div><div class="tech-flow"><div><span>Frontend</span><strong>Razor + Bootstrap</strong><small>Responsive user interface</small></div><b>→</b><div><span>Application</span><strong>ASP.NET Core MVC</strong><small>C# controllers and workflows</small></div><b>→</b><div><span>Data</span><strong>EF Core + SQL Server</strong><small>Relational persistence</small></div><b>→</b><div><span>Security</span><strong>ASP.NET Identity</strong><small>Authentication and roles</small></div></div><div class="tech-tags"><span>.NET 10</span><span>C#</span><span>Razor Views</span><span>Bootstrap</span><span>JavaScript</span><span>EF Core</span><span>SQL Server</span><span>Identity</span></div></div></section>
<section class="about-section" id="workflow"><div class="about-container"><div class="work-grid"><div><span class="about-eyebrow">OUR WORKFLOW</span><h2>From registration to completed care coordination.</h2><p>The application follows a connected workflow rather than isolated CRUD screens.</p></div><div class="work-list"><div><strong>Reception</strong><span>Register patient and coordinate appointments.</span></div><div><strong>Doctor</strong><span>Confirm, consult, document and request follow-up work.</span></div><div><strong>Laboratory</strong><span>Process tests and record results.</span></div><div><strong>Pharmacist</strong><span>Process prescriptions and maintain medicine stock.</span></div><div><strong>Patient</strong><span>View appointments, records, results, prescriptions and history.</span></div></div></div></div></section>
